# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# council/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with cad/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES
# and pcb/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# A suite going missing (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing
# unregistered is a loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
#
# The assertion count is pinned from a run that got through every section with
# the backend up. The executable pin below is the observed total; it includes
# the original sections plus the regression cases added at landing.
#
# A lower count means a setup guard fired rather than exercising its section.
#
# SETUP THIS SUITE NEEDS beyond the runner's own: section 6 drives the REAL
# backend over stdio, so council-plugin must be built first —
#     (cd council && go build -o council-plugin ./)
# and the Minerva checkout needs its `terminal` GDExtension built, like every
# other suite that starts a real plugin subprocess. Without the binary the
# section fails by name; it does not skip.

# The native panel end to end: mounted through the real PluginScenePanelHost
# from the real manifest, saved and reloaded byte-for-byte, round-tripped
# through a plugin_data note, an unreadable document preserved rather than
# replaced, the host envelope measured against the host's own cap, and two
# panels in two projects kept apart against one backend store; a document from
# an older schema migrated on open; a run saved in flight demoted on reopen and
# continued explicitly without re-asking the seat that answered; and a panel
# reopened onto a document the engine had already carried further, while a
# lagging copy opened alongside another panel is replaced rather than merged;
# and a round driven straight down the MCP tool door, with no panel in the
# exchange, reaching the panel that owns that document before it saves; and the
# one text derivation a session hands over, held to the fixture that is its
# oracle and proved to be the same text through both of its callers, including a
# session past the send lane's cap, whose messages have to concatenate back to
# that derivation byte for byte, and a block whose single line straddles the
# boundary, where a line-end cut would halve what each message carries.
# Includes four landing regressions: foreign write, pending save warning,
# delayed convergence after another panel becomes the holder, and empty-panel
# project-scoped adoption after its prior owner closes.
test_council_panel.gd assertions=125

# The per-plugin CONTRACT GUARD: six domain-defined cases (null/empty, small
# and large x happy/unhappy, and the large-with-errors complaint reply) driven
# through the real broker and the real council-plugin subprocess, with the wire
# bytes of every large case printed on the Results line. Shares only its
# assertion discipline with the other plugins' guards
# (scripts/contract_guard.gd); the six cases, and council's definition of
# "large" (transcript length), are its own. Same rig and the same setup needs
# as the suite above: the binary must be built, and the plugin REGISTRY is
# stubbed so a second runtime is never started for the same plugin id.
#
# council is the plugin whose LARGE side is the REQUEST — the whole document
# travels out on every seed — so case 4 measures the request against the
# control cap and case 5 measures it against council's OWN document budget
# (internal/session/envelope.go MaxEnvelopeBytes, 1 MiB), which the suite
# mirrors as a constant so a drift shows up as a case that no longer proves
# what it says.
#
# 30 assertions = 4 setup (host scripts, the manifest, the binary speaking, the
# panel and its bulk route) + 3 small-happy + 3 null/empty (refusal + code, the
# held document survives) + 4 small-unhappy (refusal + code, the code IS
# stale_revision, nothing moved) + 5 large-happy (the request is over the cap,
# not an oversize refusal, success, the engine accepted it, it is holding it) +
# 5 large-unhappy (the fixture is past the budget, not an oversize refusal,
# refused, the held document survives) + 5 large-with-errors (not oversize,
# refused, the complaint reply outweighs the clean one, the held document
# survives) + 1 teardown.
#
# `real-worker` is not claimed: council ships no scripts/probe-worker-methods.py
# and this suite prints no such field. Its pin describes a host with the binary
# built; without it the setup fails by name rather than skipping.
test_contract_guard.gd assertions=30
